  "dependency_tracking": {
    "_comment": "HOW DEPENDENCY TRACKING SAVES TOKENS ON UPDATES: When the script detects a changed file hash, it re-parses only that file. For each element whose content_hash changed, it sets conversion_status to 'needs_regeneration'. The dependency chain then propagates upward: if atm-primarybutton-01 changes, all molecules in its 'depended_on_by' list are also marked 'needs_regeneration', and so on up to organisms. This means on a typical incremental update — e.g., a designer tweaks one button style — only 3-5 components are regenerated instead of the full 26+. The LLM receives only those tasks, keeping the context window small and the cost low.",
